<title>HONG KONG: Lee Hing Dev 1996 net rises 67.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Lee Hing Dev 1996 net rises 67.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   57.92	vs 36.21</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    10.0	 vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  13.71 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    201.69     vs 120.56</p>
<p>    Turnover		     411.27     vs 213.86</p>
<p>    Company name		 Lee Hing Development Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 13-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 27</p>
<p>NOTE - Lee Hing Development engages in investment holdings, property investment and development and trading in listed shares.</p>
<p>The company proposed a cash bonus of four H.K. cents per share.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of interests in subsidiary companies and associated companies.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 22 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of eight cents and cash bonus) vs 18 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
